ions, as "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Il. 1.135", "author_abbreviation": "Il.", "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "140", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", etc.; ἀ. καὶ ὥς . . "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "1.116", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; ἀ. οὐδ' ὥς . . "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Od. 1.6", "author_abbreviation": "Od.", "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "002", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ":—after "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Hom.", "author_abbreviation": "Hom.", "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": " in answers and objections, nay but . . , well but . . , freq. with negs., esp. in making and answering objections, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Ar. Ach. 402", "author_abbreviation": "Ar.", "tlg_author": "0019", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "407", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0019", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; also in affirmative answers, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Pl. Prt. 330b", "author_abbreviation": "Pl.", "tlg_author": "0059", "tlg_work": "022", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Grg. 449a", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0059", "tlg_work": "023", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", etc.:—repeated in a succession of questions or objections, πότερον ᾔτουν σέ τι . . ; ἀ. ἀπῄτουν; ἀ. περὶ παιδικῶν μαχόμενος; ἀ. μεθύων ἐπαρῴνησα; "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "X. An. 5.8.4", "author_abbreviation": "X.", "tlg_author": "0032", "tlg_work": "006", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", cf. "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Pl. Thg. 123e", "author_abbreviation": "Pl.", "tlg_author": "0059", "tlg_work": "017", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Isoc. 17.47", "author_abbreviation": "Isoc.", "tlg_author": "0010", "tlg_work": "005", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; ἀ. μήν . . , answered by ἀ . . , "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Arist. Pol. 1287a23", "author_abbreviation": "Arist.", "tlg_author": "0086", "tlg_work": "035", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ":—in vehement answers "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Pl.", "author_abbreviation": "Pl.", "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": " often uses νὴ τοὺς θεοὺς ἀ . . . , μὰ Δίʼ ἀ . . , "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Grg. 481c", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0059", "tlg_work": "023", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Phlb. 36a", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0059", "tlg_work": "010", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", cf. "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Alc. 1.110b", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", c:—at beginning of speech, to introduce a general objection, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Od. 4.472", "author_abbreviation": "Od.", "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "002", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", cf."}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "X. Smp. 1", "author_abbreviation": "X.", "tlg_author": "0032", "tlg_work": "004", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Men. Georg. 22", "author_abbreviation": "Men.", "tlg_author": "0541", "tlg_work": "003", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ". with imper. or subj., to remonstrate, encourage, persuade, etc., freq. in "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Hom.", "author_abbreviation": "Hom.", "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", ἀ. ἄγε, ἴθι, "}, {"kind":